petal::route_file!(spec:petal::static_read_spec(),read:|_:&petal::Ctx|petal::read_json_value(&"Pump.fun Petal. People: open index.html in a browser from the mounted folder, or cat coins/live.md, coins/<mint>.md and trade/<wallet>/holdings.md in a terminal. Agents: list the latest and live coins under coins/, read one's price, holders and risk warnings with coins/<mint>.json and its chart and trades under market/<mint>/, see what the selected Bloom account holds in trade/<wallet>/holdings.json, then buy or sell, or launch a coin with trade/<wallet>/launch.json, or place a limit order with trade/<wallet>/limit.json (see orders.json). Every trade is one operation the owner approves in Bloom, capped at the SOL ceiling the approval shows and rebuilt with a fresh blockhash after it; there is no session key, no separate wallet, and no standing budget. Slippage defaults to 1% and is capped at 5%, swaps go through Jito's front-running protection by default, sells are priced against the chain, and a sell of \"all\" closes the emptied token account. An empty token account can also be closed on its own, returning its rent to the same account."));
